course: dictionary
lesson: 12592
title: Discard: to throw away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To discard something is to throw it away or get rid of it because you do not want or need it. «Please discard the seeds before you cook the apple.» You do not need the seeds, so you throw them away.
explain: Discard can also be a noun, meaning a thing that has already been thrown away. «The pile of discards went to the recycling bin.» The discards are the things nobody wants any more.
explain: In card games, to discard means to put down a card you do not want. «Sam discarded a two and picked up a king.» The clue is the card going down and not being kept.
fact: Discard means to throw away or get rid of something you do not want or need.
fact: As a noun, a discard is a thing that has been thrown away.
fact: In card games, to discard is to put down a card you do not want.
fact: «Discard the broken glass carefully» means throw it away, and take care because it can cut you.
exercise: «Please discard the seeds before you cook the apple.» What does discard mean here? | Plant them in the garden | Eat them slowly | *Throw them away | Keep them safe
exercise: «The pile of discards went to the recycling bin.» What are the discards? | Things that have been bought from the shop | Very large boxes | *Things that have been thrown away | Cards kept for the next game
exercise: «Sam discarded a two and picked up a king.» What is happening in this card game? | Sam won the game | *Sam put down a card he did not want | Sam kept the two for later | Sam shuffled the cards
test: Which word means the same as discard? | Hide | Polish | Keep | *Throw away
test: A scientist discards the outlier in her data. Why? | It is her favourite number | It is the first number she wrote | It makes the chart look colourful | *It does not fit the pattern, so it is removed and no longer counts
exam: Which sentence uses discard as a noun, meaning things that have been thrown away? | They discard cards quickly in the game. | She will discard the old map. | *Her pile of discards went to the charity bin. | Please discard your empty cup.
